 {"id":"CF-167","title":"P4 — docs/OPERATIONS.md offers `--server` as a substitute for `BUNKER_SERVER`, so the documented verify recipe aborts at scripts/verify-node.sh:17 before it parses a single flag","status":"complete","priority":"P4","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-04T06:41:42Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T06:49:03Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"f65c37d99d84809f42394db890ad9c0a6e721bbadc80396454d45736be838d21","evidence":[{"run_id":"a257fbd6","ts":"2026-11-04T06:49:03Z","tree_fp":"e8fcf6c1e3e7dd6cfd1d5080f49dc6b1462b77e0eedb91c39d4099fa6d634fe5","artifacts":[".gitreins/history/2026-11-04/a257fbd6/verdict.json"]}]},"reasoning":"Measured 2026-11-04 at 9b7fb6f in a clone of the published ref. docs/OPERATIONS.md §6 step 3 (:127) said \"Required environment: BUNKER_SERVER unless --server is supplied\", and §11 (:195) listed the invocation with --server NAME and no environment precondition. scripts/verify-node.sh:17 assigns SERVER=\"${BUNKER_SERVER:?…}\", so the shell expands the guard while executing that line, before the argument loop at :18-26 reads argv (:21 handles --server). Run: env -u BUNKER_SERVER ./scripts/verify-node.sh --agent probe-agent --server some-server --port 10800 -> \"./scripts/verify-node.sh: line 17: BUNKER_SERVER: set BUNKER_SERVER to your bunker server name\", rc 1, and the script never prints its \"verify node <id>\" banner. Control arm with the variable set reaches the agent_alive probe (FAIL — placeholder server), proving the flag is only consulted after the guard. Same class as CF-009/CF-041/CF-145 (documented path fails as written); distinct from CF-063, which owns relaxing the script's pre-parse guard — this row owns the prose that promises the branch. Corrected in docs/OPERATIONS.md:127 and :195 with the code path cited; evidence docs/audits/code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-verify-env.md.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Reproduce on the current tree: `env -u BUNKER_SERVER ./scripts/verify-node.sh --agent probe-agent --server some-server --port 10800; echo rc=$?` prints `./scripts/verify-node.sh: line 17: BUNKER_SERVER: set BUNKER_SERVER to your bunker server name` and `rc=1`, with no `verify node` banner.\n2. Control arm: `BUNKER_SERVER=some-server ./scripts/verify-node.sh --agent probe-agent --server some-server --port 10800` prints `verify node probe-agent` and reaches the `agent_alive` row.\n3. `grep -n 'unless .--server. is supplied' docs/OPERATIONS.md` returns no matches (exit 1) at the fixed tip.\n4. `awk 'NR==127' docs/OPERATIONS.md` names `scripts/verify-node.sh:17` and the argument loop at `:18-26`, and states the env var is required even when `--server` is passed.\n5. `awk 'NR==195' docs/OPERATIONS.md` carries the same requirement in the inventory boundary cell.\n6. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` and exits 0; `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK`.","probe":"env -u BUNKER_SERVER ./scripts/verify-node.sh --agent probe-agent --server some-server --port 10800; echo rc=$?","commit_hash":"7aaac547f56a26751a4d6c513a75e432bb6ca499","guard_result":"PASS","ci_result":"SKIP","worker_summary":"docs/OPERATIONS.md:127 and :195 corrected — BUNKER_SERVER is required even when --server is passed; code path cited (scripts/verify-node.sh:17 before the :18-26 argument loop). Evidence docs/audits/code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-verify-env.md; impl 7aaac54; verdict CF-167-DOC2 a76b817c PASS."}
 {"id":"CF-168","title":"P3 — tests/selftest.sh 7b can report a FALSE red under set -uo pipefail: printf | grep -q answers 141 on SIGPIPE after the text matched, so a passing arm grades FAIL","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-04T06:56:27Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T06:56:27Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"5d4b380b6158d0f2054bf856b0c0923886b50a4781244c44d66af2400c74798d"},"reasoning":"Observed once while gating 5fc2cbd in this lane's tick (code-factory-duckbrain-releng-2026-11-04-06-11-13): a full `bash tests/selftest.sh` run graded section 7b's `number` arm FAIL — `FAIL  number fixture escaped the board gate (exit 1)` — while the same arm printed `FAIL  board line 2: expected JSON object, got 42` and `FAIL  2 of 3 rows parse` and exited 1, i.e. every condition the arm asserts was satisfied. Two further runs at the same tree answered `SELFTEST: PASS` / 106 rows, and 20 isolated iterations of the same fixture never reproduced it, so the arm itself is not broken: the ASSERTION is.\n\nMechanism: tests/selftest.sh:3 sets `set -uo pipefail`; the arm's conditions at tests/selftest.sh:242-244 are `printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | grep -Fq ...` / `grep -Fxq ...` / `! ... | grep -q ...`. `grep -q` exits as soon as it matches, so `printf` can take SIGPIPE on its remaining write; `pipefail` then makes the pipeline answer 141 even though grep matched, the `&&` chain falls through to the else branch, and the suite prints a false FAIL and increments `fails`. Deterministic demonstration (the row's probe): a writer that prints the match first and then more lines yields `assert_rc=141` on three consecutive runs.\n\nWhy it matters: this is the inverse of the suite's own doctrine (\"a green that cannot go red is decoration\") — a red that cannot be trusted is just as useless, and a single flaky arm makes a whole tick's gate evidence ambiguous: a releng/review lane cannot distinguish a real regression from a 141, and the tidiest response (re-run until green) is exactly the habit that hides real reds. Any `grep -q` early-exit site in the suite is in the same class, so the fix should be class-level, not a one-line patch of 7b.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce the hazard on the current tree: the row's `probe` prints `assert_rc=141` and exits 0 — under `set -uo pipefail` a `printf '%s\\n' \"$out\" | grep -Fq ...` assertion can return 141 (SIGPIPE on the writer) AFTER the text matched, so the assertion grades a passing condition as a failure.\n\n1. No suite assertion depends on that shape: `grep -nE \"printf .*\\| *grep -[A-Za-z]*q\" tests/selftest.sh` lists every remaining site, and each is pipefail-safe (here-string, `case`, or `grep -c` with an explicit `|| true`) or carries a comment naming why SIGPIPE cannot occur there (single short write, no early exit). Section 7b's checks (tests/selftest.sh:242-244) are among the repaired sites.\n\n2. Both directions still proven after the repair: all nine 7b fixtures answer `PASS  <arm> fixture rejected, exit 1`, and a planted control that makes the board gate accept an invalid record still produces a `FAIL` row — a fix that turns the red arm permanently green is a regression, not a repair.\n\n3. Provenance recorded: the change's evidence names the observed false red (tick `code-factory-duckbrain-releng-2026-11-04-06-11-13`, tree `5fc2cbd`, the `FAIL  number fixture escaped the board gate (exit 1)` row and the two later `SELFTEST: PASS` runs at the same tree), so a reader can separate a real arm regression from this 141 class.\n\n4. Gate: `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` with rc 0, and `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK`.","probe":"t=$(mktemp -d); printf '%s\\n' 'set -uo pipefail' 'w() { printf \"%s\\n\" \"MATCH-LINE\"; seq 1 200000; }' 'out=$(w)' 'printf \"%s\\n\" \"$out\" | grep -Fq \"MATCH-LINE\"; echo \"assert_rc=$?\"' > \"$t/a.sh\"; bash \"$t/a.sh\"; rm -r -- \"$t\"","commit_hash":null,"guard_result":null,"ci_result":null,"worker_summary":null}
